# Firebase CLI

This project talks to Firebase through the Firebase CLI. Project: `ascend-platform-7b5f8` (`.firebaserc`). Config: `firebase.json`.

- Firestore rules: `apps/api/firestore.rules`
- Firestore indexes: `apps/api/firestore.indexes.json`
- Storage rules: `apps/api/storage.rules`

When a query needs an index, or rules need to be published, deploy from the repo. Do not hand the user a Firebase Console link as the way to create it.

```bash
firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes --project ascend-platform-7b5f8
firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --project ascend-platform-7b5f8
firebase deploy --only storage --project ascend-platform-7b5f8
```

Add a missing composite index to `apps/api/firestore.indexes.json`, then deploy indexes. A new index can take a minute or two to finish building after the deploy succeeds.
